 "summary": "The household's work as a list (JobBook reads it; SpouseCore and every other worker run it). A job takes pack kinds (inputs) from the household store and puts pack kinds (outputs) back, so the chain is derived: a job whose input is another job's output comes after it (carcass > butcher > venison > cook / smoke / jerky). The planner is pull-based: the targets say what the household should hold, a shortage pulls the jobs that fill it and, back along the chain, the jobs that feed those.",
 "stages": ["gather", "process", "preserve", "craft", "upkeep"],
 "stage_names": {"gather": "Gather", "process": "Process", "preserve": "Preserve", "craft": "Craft", "upkeep": "Upkeep"},
